This product implements RFC 7932 (Brotli Compressed Data Format).

The following data-only artifacts are derived from Google's brotli project
(https://github.com/google/brotli), which is licensed under the MIT License
(see https://github.com/google/brotli/blob/master/LICENSE):

  * Sources/Brotli/Dictionary.swift — the 122 784-byte Brotli static
    dictionary, embedded byte-for-byte from c/common/dictionary.bin.
    Source SHA-256:
    20e42eb1b511c21806d4d227d07e5dd06877d8ce7b3a817f378f313653f35c70.

  * Sources/Brotli/Transforms.swift — the 121-entry static-dictionary
    transforms table and the 50-entry prefix/suffix string pool,
    extracted from c/common/transform.c.

  * Sources/Brotli/ContextMap.swift — the four context-mode lookup tables
    (LSB6, MSB6, UTF8, Signed), each 2 × 256 bytes, extracted from
    c/common/context.c.

These are data, not Google code: swift-brotli does not bundle, link to,
or runtime-depend on the Google brotli C library, decoder, or encoder.
The algorithmic implementation in Sources/Brotli/*.swift (excluding the
three data-only files above) is a clean-room Swift implementation of
RFC 7932.
